   118	loader **accepts compressed-point SPKIs and other curves** (LIB03). The verifier's own X < p check and exact-prefix
   119	rule are what reject K-04/K-16 and K-17/K-18. Replacing `codec.point` with a library-only check flips exactly K-04 and
   120	K-16 (agent run 2026-10-27, not kept as a test because it patches the verifier in-process). The library rejects
   121	off-curve points on its own (LIB01).
   122	
   123	**ML-DSA-65 (hybrid kms).** The only check is the exact 1974-byte SPKI: OID 2.16.840.1.101.3.4.3.18, parameters
   124	absent, zero unused bits, minimal DER (K-22 accepted; K-24..K-34 `KEY_FORMAT`). There is no further public-key
   125	validation. Every 1952-byte string is a well-formed FIPS 204 key: the all-zero key is accepted (K-23), and the
   126	library accepts it too (LIB06). The library's generic DER loader would accept ML-DSA-44/-87 SPKIs as keys of their own
   127	parameter sets (LIB04); the verifier's exact-prefix rule rejects them (K-28, K-29).
